{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1114615-\u200bnarr\u00b4s-thought-and-rules-revisions-requiem-2nd-edition-humanity","id":1114615,"title":"\u200bNarr\u00b4s thought and rules revisions (Requiem 2nd edition): Humanity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-11T08:54:49-07:00","id":1114615,"title":"\u200bNarr\u00b4s thought and rules revisions (Requiem 2nd edition): Humanity","content":"<br /> So I play Requiem quite a while now, and since Blood &amp; Smoke came out, I am fallen in love for a second time. In my games, there were rules revision and houserules and I thought I can share it with you. Maybe you find some of my ideas inspirational or helpful.<br /> Naturally, it will be not for anyones taste. So I\u00b4ll start with the biggest thing for Vampire: Humanity.<br /> <br /> Don\u00b4t get me wrong. Back in the 90s, Humanity was a big new idea for a roleplaying game, it stepped on new grounds, the only rpg from that time I can think of that had the narrative dice idea was west end\u00b4s star wars.<br /> I don\u00b4t want to belittle that idea in any way.<br /> But it didn\u00b4t cut it for me. So I changed it quite a few times. Here\u00b4s the things that I came up with.<br /> <b> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>No Draugr! No downward spiral! No man vs beast!</u></b><br /> <br /> The first thing I cut was the downward spiral, as early as 98-99. Here a few short reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) Immersion Breaking: At this rate, you cannot possibly imagine a Vampire getting 500 years old without succumbing to madness.<br /> 2) Forces players to play the Vampire looking for redemption.<br /> 3) Beast vs Human is not my thing, for me, that\u00b4s for werwolfs. My topic is Vampire vs. Human<br /> <br /> So, in stories where you a vampire searches for redemption, you\u00b4ll find the conflict between the vampire who wants to remain human and that one who thinks him naive and delusional. The strong point in this story is: The &quot;evil&quot; Vampire could be right. Maybe the &quot;good&quot; Vampire is delusional. Maybe he is totally wrong how he should be.<br /> When Humanity 0 makes you a mad monster, it makes the &quot;good&quot; Vampire be totally right in his opinion. There\u00b4s no conflict and no ambiguity.<br /> <br /> So for me, a Vampire with eroding humanity does not become Beast-like. He becomes Alien, he becomes a Vampire. Humans become dolls, morality does not mean a thing to him, but he can be symathic, he can love, he can be even nice.<br /> Maybe reaching Humanity 0 is a more or less necessarily transition. Maybe Vampires who refuse that are more or less immature. You will not know. When taking away the Draugr and letting players play Vampires with Humanity 0, the answer to this question and the fight in this conflict are yours to explore.<br /> <br /> My elders have all Humanity 0-3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Play with &quot;Hell is other people&quot;!</u></b><br /> <br /> Buy Danse Macabre! Search &quot;Hell is other people&quot;! Use it in your chronicles!<br /> <br /> Seriously, &quot;Hell is other people&quot; is maybe the best thing happened to Vampire ever. It is fun, it is scary, it is horror. 2nd edition rules made great leaps forward in Humanity rules, but they cannot create the good things that come out with these rules.<br /> <br /> I will not post the full rules here, in a nutshell you have seven people that ARE your humanity points. Doing something bad and you collect steam and self- disgust. You have to unload that steam, called atrocity, on your people who are called &quot;Anchors&quot; in Danse Macabre, today we would maybe call them touchstones. When you unload, you hurt them. They will go away some day or the World of Darkness will come and consume them, because they were to near to you.<br /> <br /> It is so great because:<br /> <br /> 1) Hurting them will make the players uneasy. It is horror. Botching a frenzy roll and massacring civillains doesn\u00b4t feel like horror, but the evil you did will come back to you - with a detour. THAT\u00b4s horror.<br /> 2) You are rotten, you are a creature of the night. You can be Louis-like as much as you like, you are a f*cking Monster. And everything that is near to you will wither. It\u00b4s poetic, it\u00b4s strong and you have a reason to behave like a Vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Tweaks for &quot;Hell is other people&quot;</u></b><br /> <br /> Got a few tweaks that could interest everyone who thinks about playing with this ruleset.<br /> <br /> <b><u>New Comforts:</u></b><br /> <br /> There are not enough Comforts, IMHO. So I invented 5 new ones:<br /> <br /> <u>Advice: </u>When seeking advice to cope with a problem or a difficult situation or a piece of work, the Vampire may give one test +2 dice while solving that problem. If he has to sneak into a building, open a safe and steal something, he could first ask his anchor. While he does it, he could either give +2 to his stealth test or his Larceny test.<br /> <br /> <u>Confessor: </u>When dumping his atrocity dice and deciding before the roll that he will put the successes exclusively on Exposure,he rolls 2 dice less. He will always roll at least one die.<br /> <br /> <u>Escapism: </u>When spending several hours with the anchor, the vampire regains 1 Willpower.<br /> <br /> <u>Intimacy: </u>When the Vampire spends several hours with the Anchor, he gets +2 dice on his next frenzy roll.<br /> <br /> <u>Therapy</u>: When spending several hours with the anchor, the vampire can discard on Condition. He gets, however, no Beat for this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>10 Atrocity</b></u><br /> <br /> A permanent Atrocity die is not a good idea. It\u00b4s impractical, it\u00b4s complicated and you need to keep track of the permanent atrocity dice of the elders, who would have 1-5 atrocity dice, making them more powerful that they already are.<br /> <br /> No, scrap that. As the Bane- rule in B&amp;S does not work in a good way anyway, I propose that when you collect 10 Atrocity, go to 0 Atrocity, take a bane and a beat.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Fluid Humanity</b></u><br /> <br /> My newest idea is the fluid humanity. I figured that it would be possible to say that being a Vampire is not a downward spiral, but you change, there are phases when you are more or less human.<br /> Take an elder. He awakes from torpor, all his Anchors are dead. He has Humanity 0, he is an alien being, a Vampire. Think of Lestat. So, the alien Vampire moves through the world and meets someone special. He becomes his anchor and he is reminded of humanity. He has now humanity 1. And her brother? She loves him, he wants to protect him - Humanity 2. And so on.<br /> <br /> Maybe your humanity 3 Vampire founds someone new. It gives him back a piece of his humanity. Would explain the Vampires who suddenly stalk &quot;special&quot; girls <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> I am not totally clear, how I will do it. Maybe 4 Experience to make a Human an Anchor. Maybe you can make it through the social mechanics, although you would then loose the opportunity to get anchors that don\u00b4t know you or hate you, that would be a shame. Maybe you make it through GM and PC decision, if a human becomes important, he becomes an anchor.<br /> <br /> <br /> That\u00b4s all, folks.<br /> <br /> Keep on gaming,<br /> <br /> Dennis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}